course: dictionary
lesson: 388
title: One word, two meanings: ape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ape is a large animal with no tail, such as a gorilla, chimpanzee, bonobo, orangutan or gibbon. «Apes are usually bigger than monkeys, and they have no tail.» Ape can also be a verb: to ape someone means to copy the way they act or talk, often in a silly way.
explain: To find the right meaning, read the words around ape. If the sentence is about animals, forests or tools, it means the animal. If it is about copying someone, it means the verb. «Dad went ape when he saw the mess» is informal, so here it means he got very angry.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Ask: does «copy» fit, or does «a large animal» fit better? If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: An ape is a large primate with no tail. Gorillas, chimpanzees, bonobos, orangutans and gibbons are all apes.
fact: Apes are different from monkeys: they have no tail, they are usually bigger, and they are very clever at using tools and solving problems.
fact: Humans are classed as great apes too.
fact: To ape someone means to copy them, often in a silly way. It is a bit formal.
fact: Many apes are endangered because their forests are cut down.
exercise: «Apes cannot speak words like us, but the bonobo Kanzi learned hundreds of symbols.» What kind of animal is a bonobo? | A type of tree | *An ape | A fish | A kind of bird
exercise: Maya says, «Stop aping your big sister!» What does aping mean here? | Buying her a present | *Copying her actions in a silly way | Running very fast | Hiding from her
exercise: «Dad went ape when he saw the mess.» What does went ape mean? | He cleaned the mess quickly | *He got very excited or angry | He laughed at the mess | He climbed a tree
test: Which one is a monkey, not an ape? | *A monkey with a tail | Chimpanzee | Gorilla | Gibbon
test: «Ella aped her teacher's funny walk all the way home.» What does aped mean? | *Copied | Ignored | Painted | Cleaned
exam: Which sentence uses ape as a verb? | «The chimp swung from the branch.» | «Some apes learned hundreds of symbols.» | «Gorillas are large apes.» | *«Ben aped his brother's silly dance.»
